christoffel-symbol-lower-index-symmetry-.conceptual_definition:
The symmetry of the Christoffel symbol, expressed as $\Gamma^\sigma_{\mu
u} = \Gamma^\sigma_{
u\mu}$, is a fundamental property of the Levi-Civita connection. This connection is, by definition, torsion-free. The torsion tensor, defined as $T^\sigma_{\mu
u} = \Gamma^\sigma_{\mu
u} - \Gamma^\sigma_{
u\mu}$, vanishes for this connection, which directly implies the symmetry. This property ensures that infinitesimal parallelograms formed by parallel transport along two different vector fields will close.
